        "abstract": "In response to growing wireless demands, new WiFi standards have significantly increased the number of transmission rates. This makes it challenging to identify the optimal rate quickly. We propose WiFi-UTS, a unimodal MAB algorithm, to address this problem. As a baseline algorithm, we use the state-of-the-art rate adaptation algorithm, Minstrel-HT, and implemented Thompson sampling. The algorithms were evaluated within an RF-shielded WiFi testbed, rigorously assessing their throughput performance to showcase their efficiency under controlled conditions. Our experiments show that WiFi-UTS outperforms the baseline algorithm with an average improvement of 47% and at least 12% in all scenarios considered.",
